From: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] net: phy: qca83xx: mark EEE disabled in phylib when clearing advertisement

On QCA8327/QCA8337 switch revision 2 silicon, qca83xx_config_init() disables
EEE advertisement by clearing the MDIO_AN_EEE_ADV register (MMD 7, 0x003c)
to 0x0.

However, during phy_probe(), genphy_c45_read_eee_adv() reads the hardware
reset default (0x0006) and sets phydev->eee_enabled = true. Because
qca83xx_config_init() only cleared the hardware register without clearing
phydev->eee_enabled, subsequent calls to genphy_c45_an_config_eee_aneg()
during auto-negotiation configuration check phydev->eee_enabled and write
phydev->advertising_eee (0x0006) right back into MDIO_AN_EEE_ADV.

This leaves the PHY advertising EEE over the wire despite the driver's
intent to disable it on revision 2 silicon, leading to link instability and
receiver loss with link partners that enter LPI.

Explicitly set phydev->eee_enabled = false in case 2 of qca83xx_config_init()
so genphy_c45_an_config_eee_aneg() preserves the zeroed advertisement.

Fixes: 6b93fb664fb2 ("net-next: dsa: add new driver for QCA8K")
Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa <tomasz.figa@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca83xx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca83xx.c
@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@ static int qca83xx_config_init(struct ph
 		break;
 
 	case 2:
+		phydev->eee_enabled = false;
 		phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_AN, MDIO_AN_EEE_ADV, 0x0);
 		fallthrough;
 	case 4:
